{"uncertainty": 0.3, "outcome": "Three buckets, one per failing log. Each is a candidate RTL cause found by reading the approved RTL, not by VeriTriage. (1) data_byte_fail: data bits go out MSB first instead of LSB first. (2) parity_bit_fail: the parity bit is odd parity (~^hold) instead of even (^hold). (3) frame_period_fail: the stop bit lasts CLKS_PER_BIT/2 cycles instead of CLKS_PER_BIT. One repro testbench per bucket, each checking only its own behaviour.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "triage_report", "title": "uart_frame_tx nightly regression triage: three failures, three buckets", "summary": "Serves [requirement:req-94eee275db]. Evidence: VeriTriage session [run:run-0001] ran over data_byte_fail.log, parity_bit_fail.log and frame_period_fail.log as one combined call. It classified them as unknown_failure at 30% confidence, with 3 evidence nodes and the top hypothesis 'Likely RTL bug'. Because that is a single low-confidence class over a combined input, it is a lead only, not a bucket. The buckets below come from reading the approved RTL [artifact:prj-c391b404ed.design-under-investigation.a1], which was reviewed as fixture tests/fixtures/dv/uart_frame_tx/uart_frame_tx_buggy.v [evidence:prj-c391b404ed.design-under-investigation.e1]. The header of that file specifies even parity, LSB-first data and one stop bit of CLKS_PER_BIT cycles. BUCKET A, data_byte (signature: DATA_BIT mismatch at a data-bit position). START loads tx<=hold[7] and DATA sends hold[3'd7-next_idx], so the byte goes out MSB first. Expected fix: hold[0] then hold[next_idx]. This touches only the data-bit positions, not parity or timing. Repro: tb/repro_data_byte.v. BUCKET B, parity_bit (signature: PARITY_BIT mismatch). The design uses parity = ~^hold, which is odd parity, so the bit is inverted for every byte. Expected fix: ^hold. This is independent of bit order, since XOR is order-free. Repro: tb/repro_parity_bit.v. BUCKET C, frame_period (signature: FRAME_PERIOD shorter than 11 bit times). STOP returns to IDLE when clk_cnt==(CLKS_PER_BIT/2)-1, so the stop bit lasts 2 cycles instead of 4. Back-to-back frames start 43 clocks apart instead of at least 44. Expected fix: compare against CLKS_PER_BIT-1. Repro: tb/repro_frame_period.v, which uses data 8'h00. Bit order cannot matter for that byte, and the parity bit and stop bit are both high-or-low without adding a falling edge, so only the stop length moves the start-to-start spacing. The three causes are on separate lines of code and each breaks a different observable, so none of the buckets is merged with another. Open items: per-log VeriTriage runs, and same-seed reruns to rule out flakiness, have not been done. The log contents were not available to this seat, so the mapping from log name to cause is inferred from the log names and the RTL."}], "files": [{"path": "tb/repro_data_byte.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Repro for bucket A: data bits must be LSB first", "summary": "Self-checking repro for the data_byte failure against [artifact:prj-c391b404ed.design-under-investigation.a1], serving [requirement:req-94eee275db]. It sends 8'h01, 8'h0F, 8'hD2 and 8'h80, samples tx at mid-bit for each of the 8 data bits and compares bit i with data[i]. It checks neither parity nor stop timing. It prints the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict once before $finish.", "entry": "tb_uart_repro"}, {"path": "tb/repro_parity_bit.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Repro for bucket B: parity bit must be even parity", "summary": "Self-checking repro for the parity_bit failure against [artifact:prj-c391b404ed.design-under-investigation.a1], serving [requirement:req-94eee275db]. It sends 8'h00, 8'h01, 8'h03 and 8'hD2, samples tx in the middle of the parity bit slot and compares it with ^data. Bit order does not affect the result. It prints the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict once before $finish.", "entry": "tb_uart_repro"}, {"path": "tb/repro_frame_period.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Repro for bucket C: back-to-back frames at least 11 bit times apart", "summary": "Self-checking repro for the frame_period failure against [artifact:prj-c391b404ed.design-under-investigation.a1], serving [requirement:req-94eee275db]. It holds start high with data 8'h00 and measures the time between successive start-bit falling edges, which must be at least 11*CLKS_PER_BIT clocks. A short stop bit makes the spacing shorter. It prints the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict once before $finish.", "entry": "tb_uart_repro"}], "tool_runs": ["run:run-0001"], "claims": ["Each bucket's root cause was identified by reading the RTL source, not by a VeriTriage result; the VeriTriage session returned unknown_failure at 30% confidence.", "The assignment of each failing log to a cause is inferred from the log file names; the log contents were not available to this seat.", "Expected on the approved buggy RTL: repro_data_byte fails at least one DATA_BIT check, repro_parity_bit fails all four PARITY_BIT checks, and repro_frame_period measures a 43-clock spacing, below the 44-clock minimum. None of these simulations has been run by this seat.", "Expected on a corrected RTL: each repro passes all of its checks, and each repro fails only on its own bucket's bug. This has not been run."], "escalation": null, "notes": "All three testbenches use the same top module name, tb_uart_repro, so that the top is correct whether the platform takes it from the first file's entry or from each file's own entry. Each run compiles the RTL with one testbench. Sample points sit 25 ns into each bit relative to the posedge that drops the start bit, which keeps them off the 10 ns clock edges. Each testbench has a watchdog that counts a timeout as a failed check and prints the single verdict. Recommended follow-ups: run veritriage.investigate on each log on its own, and rerun each failure with the same seed to rule out flakiness."}

